<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Image decisions · 14 specialized models · 200 questions</title><style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;color:#183044;background:#f3f7fa;font:17px/1.65 system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif}main{max-width:1480px;margin:auto;padding:32px 42px 90px;background:white}h1{font-size:clamp(30px,4vw,48px);line-height:1.13;max-width:1050px;letter-spacing:-.03em}h2{margin-top:2.4em;line-height:1.25;color:#163e5b}h3{margin-top:1.8em}p,li{max-width:1100px}a{color:#06669a}nav{position:sticky;top:0;background:#123d58;color:white;z-index:5;padding:12px 28px;display:flex;gap:24px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:14px}nav a{color:white;text-decoration:none}img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;margin:24px 0}table{border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0;width:100%;font-size:15px;line-height:1.45;margin:18px 0 32px}th,td{padding:13px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid #dce5eb;text-align:right;vertical-align:middle}th{color:#183c56;background:#edf3f7}th:first-child,td:first-child{text-align:left}thead th{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:2}tbody tr:hover td,tbody tr:hover th{outline:1px solid #8199aa;outline-offset:-1px}small{display:block;font-weight:400;margin-top:5px;font-size:12px;color:#526b80}.table-scroll{overflow:auto;max-width:100%;margin:18px 0 36px;max-height:780px;border:1px solid #dce5eb;border-radius:10px}.table-scroll table{margin:0;min-width:840px}.family-table{table-layout:fixed}.family-table th:first-child{width:220px;position:sticky;left:0;z-index:1}.family-table thead th:first-child{z-index:3}.family-table td{font-weight:650;font-size:19px;text-align:center}.family-table thead th{text-align:center;min-width:140px}.filter{display:block;background:#edf5fa;border-radius:8px;padding:15px}input{font:inherit;border:1px solid #93adbf;border-radius:6px;padding:9px 12px;margin-left:12px}pre{overflow:auto;padding:20px;background:#edf3f7;border-radius:9px;font-size:14px}code{font-size:.88em}details{margin:24px 0}footer{font-size:13px;margin-top:50px;color:#587083}@media(max-width:700px){main{padding:20px 16px 60px}nav{gap:14px;padding:10px 16px;font-size:12px}body{font-size:16px}th,td{padding:10px}input{margin:8px 0 0;width:100%}}</style></head><body><nav><a href="#">Overview</a><a href="#overall-results">Scores, speed & cost</a><a href="#results-by-named-category">Named categories</a><a href="#excluded-routes-and-eligibility">Exclusions</a><a href="gallery.html">Questions & images</a><a href="https://github.com/etsabary/visual-decision-benchmark">GitHub evidence</a></nav><main><h1>Image-grounded System 1 decision benchmark</h1>
<p>Amos 1 Large recorded the highest image score: <strong>159/200 (79.5%)</strong>, with a <strong>340 ms median</strong> complete response. d3-turbo followed at <strong>155/200 (77.5%)</strong>, then Perplexity Decider v1.2 at <strong>152/200 (76%)</strong>. All three returned usable typed choices on every question. These are the highest observed scores in this bank, not a universal intelligence ranking.</p>
<p>The expanded comparison now contains <strong>14 specialized decision models</strong>, each measured on the same 200 image-grounded questions. Twelve completed new runs on October 20; Jev 1.14 and Luna Decisions retain their completed October 15 results. Span- 02 crossed the prespecified two-second median limit and was stopped; ScaleDown's current route rejected images. The earlier general LLM runs remain accessible as reference results rather than the focus of the current comparison.</p>
<p><a href="https://etsabary.github.io/visual-decision-benchmark/report.html">Open the readable, colour-coded report</a></p>
<p><img alt="Accuracy, speed and cost for the native decision models" src="native_images_2026-10-20/overview.png" /></p>
