<ul>
<li><strong><a href="questions/V01.md">V01 Attribute binding and set logic</a></strong>: Find objects that satisfy several visible properties at once.</li>
<li><strong><a href="questions/V02.md">V02 Conditional counting</a></strong>: Count only the objects meeting the stated visual rule.</li>
<li><strong><a href="questions/V03.md">V03 Spatial relationships</a></strong>: Apply left/right, above/below or relative-position constraints.</li>
<li><strong><a href="questions/V04.md">V04 Connectivity and reachability</a></strong>: Follow connected paths or directed arrows between nodes.</li>
<li><strong><a href="questions/V05.md">V05 Navigation and planning</a></strong>: Choose a feasible route under movement and obstacle rules.</li>
<li><strong><a href="questions/V06.md">V06 Rotation and reflection</a></strong>: Recognize the result of a rotation or mirror transformation.</li>
<li><strong><a href="questions/V07.md">V07 Geometry, folding and fit</a></strong>: Reason about shapes, folds, dimensions or what fits.</li>
<li><strong><a href="questions/V08.md">V08 Visual rule application</a></strong>: Infer or apply a rule across symbols and pictured patterns.</li>
<li><strong><a href="questions/V09.md">V09 Sequential state tracking</a></strong>: Track how successive visible actions change a state.</li>
<li><strong><a href="questions/V10.md">V10 Constraint satisfaction</a></strong>: Find the arrangement satisfying all the stated restrictions.</li>
<li><strong><a href="questions/V11.md">V11 Flowcharts and decision trees</a></strong>: Follow conditional branches to their final outcome.</li>
<li><strong><a href="questions/V12.md">V12 Causal and counterfactual reasoning</a></strong>: Determine what changes when a pictured condition is altered.</li>
<li><strong><a href="questions/V13.md">V13 Charts and quantitative comparisons</a></strong>: Read plotted values and compare or calculate the required quantity.</li>
<li><strong><a href="questions/V14.md">V14 Document reconciliation</a></strong>: Combine entries across forms, receipts or tables and apply a rule.</li>
<li><strong><a href="questions/V15.md">V15 Interface state decisions</a></strong>: Choose an action or identify a state from a screenshot.</li>
<li><strong><a href="questions/V16.md">V16 Inspection against a reference</a></strong>: Compare an object or scene against a supplied reference.</li>
<li><strong><a href="questions/V17.md">V17 Matching across images</a></strong>: Identify a corresponding object across two or three images.</li>
<li><strong><a href="questions/V18.md">V18 Image and text consistency</a></strong>: Check whether a written claim agrees with the visible evidence.</li>
<li><strong><a href="questions/V19.md">V19 Perspective and knowledge tracking</a></strong>: Apply line-of-sight constraints or track what an observer has seen.</li>
<li><strong><a href="questions/V20.md">V20 Insufficient evidence</a></strong>: Recognize when the image cannot determine the requested answer.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Excluded routes and eligibility</h2>
