<p>Span's 21-question partial accuracy is reported only in the evidence; it is not comparable to a full-bank score. ScaleDown's catalog advertises image input, but its pinned route returned HTTP 400 rejecting <code>image_url</code> parts. No caption or OCR replacement was used. Nimble, Microsoft Decision, Drex, Kev, Tev and Solar have no documented native-image route in the current reviewed access. A successful response to encoded image-shaped JSON alone is not proof of pixel decoding. See the <a href="native_images_2026-10-20/image_capabilities.json">dated capability review</a>.</p>
<h2>Bank, reference results and limitations</h2>
<p>The bank contains <strong>20 categories × 10 questions</strong>, using 227 tested compressed image files (177 single-image questions, 19 pairs and four triples). There are 187 reasoning/grounded-decision questions and 13 perception controls. Options vary: 64 questions have five choices, 135 have four, and one has three. Uniform guessing therefore averages <strong>23.44%</strong>, not 20% or 25% for every question.</p>
<p>The existing C1 preparation reduced 75.73 MiB to 54.36 MiB (28.2% fewer bytes). No images were recompressed or resized for this expansion. Smaller file size does not necessarily mean fewer billed image tokens. <strong>221 of 227 images are redistributable in this packet</strong>; six Our World in Data charts remain withheld pending third-party source-terms review. Their original private snapshots were used in all scored runs, not replacement downloads. Public hashes, source links, questions and results remain available.</p>
<p>The supplied key was kept outside execution and unchanged during these runs. Offline scoring reproduces <strong>all five original model totals</strong>, including the archived LLMs. This is a consistency check against the existing reference, not a new independent verification of every gold answer. A 10/10 category score has a wide uncertainty interval and is not a reliability certificate. No image file is shared across primary questions and the manifest assigns 200 scene groups, but source collections and task types recur. Item-level confidence intervals and pairwise tests should not be read as independent population estimates.</p>
<p><a href="questions/README.md">Browse questions and source images</a> · <a href="gallery.html">Image gallery</a> · <a href="THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md">Attribution and licenses</a> · <a href="native_images_2026-10-20/summary.json">Expanded evidence</a> · <a href="native_images_2026-10-20/family_scores.csv">Family CSV</a> · <a href="native_images_2026-10-20/attempts.jsonl">Native route ledger</a> · <a href="native_images_2026-10-20/compatibility_probes.jsonl">Admission probes</a> · <a href="native_images_2026-10-20/model_manifests.json">Model identities</a> · <a href="native_images_2026-10-20/audit_receipt.json">Audit receipt</a>.</p>
<p>The three earlier general LLM runs are preserved in the <a href="https://github.com/etsabary/visual-decision-benchmark/blob/433f9368c7e3f594febf7f42c6cefaae75cafca7/README.md">original five-model report</a> and <a href="results/summary.json">original results</a>: regular Luna 117/200, Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite 75/200 and GPT-5.4 nano 70/200. They are not deleted, rescored, or silently replaced. They are outside the current specialized-model ranking and graphics; they are not frontier LLM references.</p>
<p>The separate <a href="https://github.com/etsabary/system-1-decision-benchmark">System 1 text benchmark</a> uses 1,342 text questions. Its percentages and image percentages must not be combined into one score.</p>
<h2>Offline verification</h2>
<pre><code class="language-bash">python3 validate.py
python3 validate_native_images.py
python3 -m unittest -v test_benchmark test_image_models_2026_10_20 test_native_analysis test_native_publication
# Optional, with the original external key; never needed for API execution:
python3 score_native_images.py --answer-key /path/to/reference_key.jsonl
</code></pre>
<p>The original checksums remain intact, with superseded presentation files preserved under <code>archive_2026-10-16/</code>. The new release has a separate seal. Public validation checks file integrity, input identity, allowed choices, coverage, timing and exact-decimal costs, without network calls or credentials. Re-scoring requires the external key. Six withheld charts prevent complete request-body reconstruction using the public images alone; no validator substitutes new chart versions.</p><footer>Reviewed image benchmark · October 20, 2026 · Exact source and result records on GitHub.</footer></main><script>for(const h of document.querySelectorAll('h2'))h.id=h.textContent.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g,'-').replace(/-$/,'');
function tint(v){const a=[255,244,208],b=[24,63,122];return `rgb(${a.map((x,i)=>Math.round(x+(b[i]-x)*v)).join(',')})`}
for(const c of document.querySelectorAll('.accuracy')){const v=+c.dataset.ratio;c.style.background=tint(v);c.style.color=v>=.65?'white':'#183044'}
document.querySelector('#model-filter').addEventListener('input',e=>{const q=e.target.value.toLowerCase();for(const r of document.querySelectorAll('[data-model]'))r.hidden=!r.dataset.model.toLowerCase().includes(q)});
for(const t of document.querySelectorAll('table:not(.family-table)')){const wrap=document.createElement('div');wrap.className='table-scroll';t.before(wrap);wrap.append(t)}
const overall=[...document.querySelectorAll('table')].find(t=>t.querySelector('thead')?.textContent.includes('Actual 200 cost'));
if(overall){for(const r of overall.tBodies[0].rows){const a=parseFloat(r.cells[2].textContent)/100;r.cells[2].style.background=tint(a);r.cells[2].style.color=a>=.65?'white':'#183044';
for(const i of [4,5,6]){const ms=parseFloat(r.cells[i].textContent)*1000;r.cells[i].style.background=ms<=500?'#d9efdf':ms<=1000?'#fff0be':ms<=2000?'#ffe0c9':'#f6d3da'}
const text=r.cells[8].textContent;if(text.includes('Free')){r.cells[8].style.background='#edf0f3'}else{const v=parseFloat(text.replace(/[^0-9.]/g,''));r.cells[8].style.background=v<=.05?'#d9efdf':v<=.15?'#fff0be':v<=.5?'#ffe0c9':'#f6d3da'}}}
</script></body></html>